{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793402836,"nonce":"ZrP5JIv9Jz7txIu5mHMrDKrDWg8=","message":"rayde-runner's service is now generic over its sandbox backend: start(config) builds the MSB backend and checks its version, start_with(config, backend) runs the same service on any SandboxProvider (Running\u003cP\u003e defaults to Running\u003cMsb\u003e, so main.rs and the real-MSB test are unchanged). The in-memory Fake gained with_program, which stands in for a guest program in both spawn and run, so a test can play the session bridge. New native/runner/tests/service.rs drives the real HTTP service on the Fake with no VM: open creates one labelled sandbox with its own volumes; opening again reuses it and returns the same connection; a lost sandbox is recovered onto the same volumes with generation plus one and a new token; a recovery whose volume is gone refuses and creates nothing; two workspaces are isolated and deleting one removes only its sandbox and volumes; the workspace limit answers 429. A mutation check confirms the empty-disks test fails if recovery is allowed to create volumes. Real MSB on the NUC still passes after the change: the runner's end-to-end test on the Alpine path (12 s) and the toolchain path (20 s), NUC left clean. Not covered by the Fake tests: the websocket relay through the bridge, and the toolchain restore path. Next candidates: the relay test with the scripted bridge, a Fake that models the identity check on the volumes, and the dynASB Linux bring-up.","files":null}]}